<myopenmath xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" id="1468733">
<statement>
<p>Solve this system of equations using elimination.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{3}{x}-{8}{y}={27}</m> </p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{6}{x}+{9}{y}=-{21}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8"/></p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle{\left({1},-{3}\right)}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p>We chose (for no special reason) to use the first equation to eliminate x from the second equation.</p>
<p>To eliminate we need the scaled version of equation one to have a coefficient of -6. So we scale by <m>\displaystyle-\frac{{6}}{{3}}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-\frac{{{6}}}{{3}}{\left({3}{x}+-{8}{y}\right)}=-\frac{{{6}}}{{3}}{\left({27}\right)}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle-{\left({6}\right)}{x}+{16}{y}=-{54}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{6}{x}+{9}{y}=-{21}</m></p>
<p>Adding these two equations gives us</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{25}{y}=-{75}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{y}=-\frac{{75}}{{25}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{y}=-{3}</m></p>
<p>Finally we can substitute this y value into the first equation to solve for x.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{3}{x}+-{8}{\left(-{3}\right)}={27}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{3}{x}+{\left({24}\right)}={27}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{3}{x}={27}-{\left({24}\right)}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{3}{x}={3}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}=\frac{{3}}{{3}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{x}={1}</m></p>
<p>Thus the answer is <m>\displaystyle{\left({1},-{3}\right)}</m>.</p>
</solution>
</myopenmath>